A valid file passes and is shown as the loader resolved it.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy good.toml
good.toml is valid
  hard stop: on, at least 3 trusted collaborator(s)
  allow bot@example.test: keys 1A2B3C4D5E6F7A8B; pr_authors opener

```

With no path, `pcu.toml` in the current directory is checked.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy
pcu.toml is valid
  hard stop: on, at least 2 trusted collaborator(s)
  no allow-list entries

```

An unknown key fails.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy unknown_key.toml
? failed
...
Error: Invalid verify-signatures policy: unknown_key.toml: TOML parse error[..]
...

```

A misspelt table name fails instead of leaving the default policy in force.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy misspelt_table.toml
? failed
...
Error: Invalid verify-signatures policy: misspelt_table.toml: no [verify_signatures] section, so the default policy would apply (is the table name misspelt?)
...

```

A file that is not there fails.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy absent.toml
? failed
...
Error: Invalid verify-signatures policy: absent.toml: [..]
...

```

The check cannot be combined with the verify options.

```console
$ pcu verify-signatures --check-policy --post-comment --pr-number 1
? 2
error: the argument '--check-policy [<PATH>]' cannot be used with:
  --post-comment
...

```
